loper.apple.com/published/42c350caa5e5117d40d45ac28c258832/sf-three-layers-primary%402x.png","line":23,"embedded":true},{"title":"An image of the cloud sun rain fill symbol. The sun is black and the raindrops and cloud are gray to indicate that the sun is in the secondary layer.","target":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/9acc461ef73c512ab21e4713fcdc75a3/sf-three-layers-secondary%402x.png","line":25,"embedded":true},{"title":"An image of the cloud sun rain fill symbol. The raindrops are black and the sun and cloud are gray to indicate that the raindrops are in the primary layer.","target":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/f2ec783b9aedc7f59c3485efb83fbb94/sf-three-layers-tertiary%402x.png","line":27,"embedded":true},{"title":"An image of the cloud sun rain fill symbol that uses three different opacities of the system blue color in the symbol’s three different layers: the cloud is fully opaque, the sun is about 50% opaque, and the raindrops are about 25% opaque.","target":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/35fe9f56dee989f094845e640951fef5/sf-three-layers-color%402x.png","line":31,"embedded":true},{"title":"Custom symbols","target":"https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/sf-symbols#Custom-symbols","line":33},{"title":"A diagram showing a row of eight symbols, all of which use a single opacity of the system blue color.","target":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/b296a9ee1b06b49c011209c83b537096/sf-monochrome%402x.png","line":39,"embedded":true},{"title":"A diagram showing a row of eight symbols, each of which uses different opacities of the system blue color. From the left, the square and arrow up symbol uses full opacity for the arrow and low opacity in the square. Next, folder badge plus uses full opacity for the badge and low opacity for the folder. Trash slash uses full opacity for the slash and low opacity for the can. Calendar day timeline right uses full opacity for the horizontal indicator and low opacity for the square and dots. List number uses full opacity for the column of numbers and low opacity for the horizontal lines. Text format A B C dotted underline uses full opacity for the dots under the low-opacity letters. iPhone radio waves left and right uses full opacity for the device outline, mid opacity in the screen area, and low opacity for the radio wave lines. Lastly, the PC symbol uses full opacity for the device outline and the onscreen sad face and horizontal lines and mid opacity in the screen background.","target":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/c035476f6266b094b051d4e392329092/sf-hierarchical%402x.png","line":43,"embedded":true},{"title":"A diagram showing a row of eight symbols, each of which uses a combination of gray and the system blue color. From the left, the square and arrow up symbol uses blue for the arrow and light gray for the square. Next, folder badge plus uses blue for the badge and light gray for the folder. Trash slash uses blue for the slash and light gray for the can. Calendar day timeline right uses blue for the horizontal indicator and light gray for the square and dots. List number uses blue for the column of numbers and light gray for the horizontal lines. Text format A B C dotted underline uses blue for the dots under the light gray letters. iPhone radio waves left and right uses blue for the device outline, medium gray in the screen area, and light gray for the radio wave lines. Lastly, the PC symbol uses blue for the device outline and the onscreen sad face and horizontal lines and medium gray in the screen background.","target":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/5ea6a976464ec36e5dbdbf30588a25e0/sf-palette%402x.png","line":47,"embedded":true},{"title":"A diagram showing a row of eight symbols, using combinations of various colors. From the left, the square and arrow up symbol uses blue for all lines. Next, folder badge plus uses green for the badge and blue for the folder. Trash slash uses red for both the slash and the can. Calendar day timeline right uses red for the horizontal indicator, dark gray for the square, and light gray for the dots. List number uses black for the column of numbers and medium gray for the horizontal lines. Text format A B C dotted underline uses red for the dots under the black letters. iPhone radio waves left and right uses blue for all lines. Lastly, the PC symbol uses yellow for the device outline, white for the onscreen sad face and horizontal lines, and blue in the screen background.","target":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/82097ab3d98f098d12935ab4d6c1c896/sf-multicolor%402x.png","line":51,"embedded":true},{"title":"renderingMode(_:)","target":"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/swiftui/image/renderingmode\\(_:\\","line":53},{"title":"Gradients","target":"https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/sf-symbols#Gradients","line":57},{"title":"The sun symbol with a solid yellow fill.","target":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/2df52fad04d6250f02143138ff76da14/sf-symbols-sun-solid-fill%402x.png","line":61,"embedded":true},{"title":"The sun symbol with a gradient fill derived from a single yellow source color. The gradient color is bright on the left edge of the symbol, and subtly darkens as it approaches the right edge.","target":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/18a48b9b3b9f3842ff42f1331edeb5fb/sf-symbols-sun-gradient-fill%402x.png","line":63,"embedded":true},{"title":"Variable color","target":"https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/sf-symbols#Variable-color","line":65},{"title":"A diagram showing four versions of the speaker wave three symbol, each of which displays color in a different number of wave paths. From the left, the number of waves with color is zero, one, two, and three.","target":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/e03af602ef484d26ff5cc3428e98079a/sf-variable-color%402x.png","line":71,"embedded":true},{"title":"Weights and scales","target":"https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/sf-symbols#Weights-and-scales","line":77},{"title":"A diagram showing the square and arrow up symbol in all 27 weights and scales.","target":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/a46e2c294c605c4f5e5f626c67d6bb2d/sf-scales-weights%402x.png","line":81,"embedded":true},{"title":"A diagram showing the first of three images of the plus circle symbol followed by the capitalized word add. In each image, the word uses the same size, but the symbol uses a different size. The symbol size is small in this image. Two parallel horizontal lines appear across all three images. The top line shows the height of the capital letter A and the bottom line is the baseline under the word add. In this small symbol, the circle touches both lines.","target":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/bf6a6d81c531a772bbe9c768af32f0b8/sf-symbol-scale-small%402x.png","line":87,"embedded":true},{"title":"The second of three images of the plus circle symbol followed by the capitalized word add. In this medium symbol, the circle extends slightly above and below the lines.","target":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/aa672f59358a8bb354e4ea9e7d258467/sf-symbol-scale-medium%402x.png","line":89,"embedded":true},{"title":"The third of three images of the plus circle symbol followed by the capitalized word add. In this large symbol, the vertical line of the plus sign almost touches both lines.","target":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/6696a9dbf59f8ef7118ac712067de2e6/sf-symbol-scale-large%402x.png","line":91,"embedded":true},{"title":"`NSImage.SymbolConfiguration`","target":"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/AppKit/NSImage/SymbolConfiguration-swift.class","line":93},{"title":"`imageScale(_:)`","target":"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/SwiftUI/View/imageScale\\(_:\\","line":93},{"title":"`UIImage.SymbolScale`","target":"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/UIKit/UIImage/SymbolScale","line":93},{"title":"Design variants","target":"https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/sf-symbols#Design-variants","line":95},{"title":"A diagram showing two rows of the same five symbols. In the top row, every symbol uses the outline variant; the bottom row shows the fill variant of each symbol. From the left, the symbols are heart, heart slash, heart circle, heart square, and a heart in a rectangle.","target":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/c4486c6d1dc36ea164665276e912139a/sf-variants%402x.png","line":103,"embedded":true},{"title":"Images","target":"https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/right-to-left#Images","line":105},{"title":"A diagram with eight rows of the same twelve symbols, where each row shows a localized version of the symbol. From the left the symbols are doc rich text, doc rich text fill, character book closed, character book closed fill, character bubble, character bubble fill, character, text format superscript, text format subscript, text format size, character text box, and character cursor I beam.","target":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/cf9d526c8f3a39b600f0226125a2b228/sf-localized%402x.png","line":107,"embedded":true},{"title":"Animations","target":"https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/sf-symbols#Animations","line":122},{"title":"Custom symbols","target":"https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/sf-symbols#Custom-symbols","line":126},{"title":"Symbols","target":"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/Symbols","line":126},{"title":"`SymbolEffect`","target":"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/Symbols/SymbolEffect","line":126},{"title":"Branding","target":"https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/branding","line":237},{"title":"Custom symbols","target":"https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/sf-symbols#Custom-symbols","line":239},{"title":"Creating custom symbol images for your app","target":"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/UIKit/creating-custom-symbol-images-for-your-app","line":241},{"title":"Icons","target":"https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/icons","line":262},{"title":"VoiceOver","target":"https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/voiceover","line":272},{"title":"Platform considerations","target":"https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/sf-symbols#Platform-considerations","line":276},{"title":"Resources","target":"https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/sf-symbols#Resources","line":280},{"title":"Related","target":"https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/sf-symbols#Related","line":282},{"title":"Download SF Symbols","target":"https://developer.apple.com/sf-symbols/","line":284},{"title":"Typography","target":"https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/typography","line":286},{"title":"Icons","target":"https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/icons","line":288},{"title":"Developer documentation","target":"https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/sf-symbols#Developer-documentation","line":290},{"title":"Symbols","target":"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/Symbols","line":292},{"title":"Configuring and displaying symbol images in your UI","target":"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/UIKit/configuring-and-displaying-symbol-images-in-your-ui","line":294},{"title":"Creating custom symbol images for your app","target":"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/UIKit/creating-custom-symbol-images-for-your-app","line":296},{"title":"Videos","target":"https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/sf-symbols#Videos","line":298},{"title":"![","target":"https://devimages-cdn.apple.com/wwdc-services/images/3055294D-836B-4513-B7B0-0BC5666246B0/4F1E5BC7-921E-46C0-927A-D84295787A94/9994_wide_250x141_1x.jpg","line":300},{"title":"Change log","target":"https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/sf-symbols#Change-log","line":302}],"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[],"key":"ai stuff/antigravity-awesome-skills-main/plugins/antigravity-bundle-apple-platform-design/skills/hig-foundations/references/sf-symbols.md"},